#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# coulomb_h2

#% text
# `coulomb_h2(l, eta, rho)` gives the incoming Coulomb wave function `H-_l(eta, rho) = G_l(eta, rho) - i F_l(eta, rho)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `H-_l = H+_l - 2 i F_l` (DLMF 33.2.7-33.2.8); for real arguments it is the complex conjugate of `H+_l`.

#% item
# At `eta = 0`, `H-_l(0, rho) = -i rho h2_l(rho)`; `H-_0(0, rho) = e^(-i rho)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
coulomb_h2(1, 0.8, 5.0)
#% output
#= -0.6894148261070179 - 0.8924295006754951im

#% cell
n(coulomb_h2(3, 2, 5), 25)
#% output
#= 2.04869471377719559294238463661 - 0.431315931140878690123879600042im

#% cell
coulomb_h2(0, 0, r)
#% output
#= exp(-im*r)

#% cell
coulomb_h2(1, 0.8, 5.0) - conjugate(coulomb_h1(1, 0.8, 5.0))
#% output
#= 0.0 + 0.0im

